{start_of_chorus}
[G]Speed, bonnie [Em]boat, like a [C]bird on the [G]wing,
[Em]"Onward!" the [Am]sailors [D]cry;
[G]Carry the [Em]lad that's [C]born to be [G]King
[Em]Over the [D]sea to [G]Skye.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[Em]Loud the winds [Am]howl, [Em]loud the waves [Am]roar,
[Em]Thunderclaps [C]rend the [D]air;
[Em]Baffled, our [Am]foes [Em]stand by the [Am]shore,
[Em]Follow they [D]will not [Em]dare.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[Em]Though the waves [Am]leap, [Em]soft shall ye [Am]sleep,
[Em]Ocean's a [C]royal [D]bed.
[Em]Rocked in the [Am]deep, [Em]Flora will [Am]keep
[Em]Watch by your [D]weary [Em]head.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
[Em]Many's the [Am]lad fought [Em]on that [Am]day,
[Em]Well the clay[C]more could [D]wield,
[Em]When the night [Am]came, [Em]silently [Am]lay
[Em]Dead on Cul[D]loden's [Em]field.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
